  "body": "### What this PR does / why we need it?\r\n\r\nFixes a packed HCCL weight-transfer race when double-buffer slots are reused across NPU streams. The producer now caches per-device streams, enqueues packing and broadcast on the same buffer stream, keeps each in-flight buffer alive until that slot is synchronized, and drains all buffer streams before returning.\r\n\r\n### Does this PR introduce any user-facing change?\r\n\r\nNo API change. This fixes correctness for asynchronous packed weight updates while retaining double-buffering.\r\n\r\n### How was this patch tested?\r\n\r\n- HCCL Qwen3-30B-A3B validation passed for both packed and unpacked modes; inference used NPUs 0-3 and trainer used NPUs 4-7. Baseline and post-update outputs were identical.\n\n- vLLM main: https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/84030bbe3d74d99bad477a3d2e37a973ccd8865c\n",
